Task 4.1: Layer richer textures into existing SFX

What: play() now layers a quieter sub-octave shadow under every SFX
note (warmer body, same recognizable pitch signatures, same exported
signatures). New gated texture() + burst() helpers add quiet filtered
noise where it sells the moment: pop/snap/pop-bubble clicks, footstep
scuffs, munch crunches, a fizzy bath bed, and shimmer tails on
star/sparkle. Volumes stay gentle (0.012-0.03); mute/bedtime gating
unchanged (silence still constructs nothing - no context, no
oscillators, no noise sources).

Tests: Red-first - updated count assertions for the doubled oscillator
layering (munch 6, footsteps >=8, fizz+yawn 14, pop-bubble 2, puzzle
cumulative 2/6/10, sparkle >=8, giggle+star+fanfare 18) plus a new
'sfx textures' suite (5 cases: noise beds, tails, clicks, grainy
texture, silence creates zero sources). One miscalibrated Red
expectation (sparkle >=9 assumed a fifth note that does not exist)
corrected to >=8 - the sparkle richness comes from its noise tail.

Full suite: 208/208. pnpm check clean.

